IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mai-core`
IMPORT `mai-seat`
IMPORT `mai-seat-insurer`

-- Cases for the relevant insurer's seat (mai-seat-insurer.l4), mirror cases against the individual's seat
-- (mai-seat.l4), and the regulative rules of the core (mai-core.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited Act (A2019-12.txt) and Declaration (NI2026-402.txt),
-- never copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comment above each assertion.
-- MIRROR CASES: the same facts asked from both seats, asserted equal to the hand-worked answer and to each other.
-- REGULATIVE RULES: a breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so rules are asserted
-- where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days. A LEST or
-- HENCE rule starts at the event that shows a deadline has passed, and that event is not matched against it; so a
-- trace waits (WAITUNTIL) to the day after a deadline before the next act.
-- HYPOTHETICAL throughout; no scenario life raised this Act.

`3 Aug 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 8 2026
`10 Aug 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 8 2026
`17 Aug 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 8 2026
`20 Aug 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 8 2026
`25 Aug 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 25 8 2026
`1 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026
`22 Sep 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 22 9 2026
`23 Sep 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 23 9 2026
`1 Oct 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2026
`5 Oct 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 10 2026
`10 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 10 2026
`15 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 10 2026
`20 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 10 2026
`2 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 11 2026
`3 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 11 2026
`9 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 9 11 2026
`15 Nov 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 11 2026
`18 Nov 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 18 11 2026
`1 Dec 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2026
`11 Dec 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 11 12 2026
`30 Dec 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 12 2026
`1 Apr 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027
`1 Oct 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2027
`3 Aug 2028`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 8 2028
`3 Aug 2031`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 8 2031
`10 May 2059` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 5 2059

`ongoing` MEANS `in paid work as an ongoing employee or fixed term contractor (s 81)`
`casual short` MEANS `in paid work, casually, with fewer than 260 hours in the 52 weeks before`
`IRB` MEANS `income replacement benefits or treatment and care benefits`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- MIRROR CASE 1. Mia (as in mai-cases-injured.l4): injured 3 August 2026, ongoing employee, 34, pension age 10 May
-- 2059; applies 20 August 2026; insurer receives it that day; HYPOTHETICAL guideline period 5 days; receipt notice
-- 25 August 2026. Pre-injury income $1 500, super paid, SG 12.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 60 (1): 25 August 2026, both seats.
#ASSERT `By when must I give the receipt notice` `20 Aug 2026` 5 EQUALS `25 Aug 2026`
#ASSERT `By when must I give the receipt notice` `20 Aug 2026` 5 EQUALS `By when must the insurer give me a receipt notice` `20 Aug 2026` 5
-- s 65 (1): 22 September 2026, both seats.
#ASSERT `By when must I decide liability` `25 Aug 2026` EQUALS `22 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT `By when must I decide liability` `25 Aug 2026` EQUALS `By when must the insurer decide liability` `25 Aug 2026`
-- s 65 (4): no notice by 22 September; on 23 September the insurer is taken to have accepted. Both seats.
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `no notice given yet` `23 Sep 2026` `23 Sep 2026` EQUALS `taken to have accepted liability: no transfer or rejection notice within 28 days after the receipt notice (s 65 (4))`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `no notice given yet` `23 Sep 2026` `23 Sep 2026` EQUALS `Has the insurer accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `no notice given yet` `23 Sep 2026` `23 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `a rejection notice: liability not accepted` `22 Sep 2026` `23 Sep 2026` EQUALS `liability rejected (s 65 (3) (b))`
-- The insurer's acceptance (or deemed acceptance) as a yes/no.
#ASSERT `the relevant insurer has accepted, or is taken to have accepted, liability` (`Am I taken to have accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `no notice given yet` `23 Sep 2026` `23 Sep 2026`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the relevant insurer has accepted, or is taken to have accepted, liability` (`Am I taken to have accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `a transfer notice: another insurer is liable` `1 Sep 2026` `23 Sep 2026`))

-- s 96, 1 September 2026: 1500 x 0.95 = 1425 a week, 2850 a fortnight. Both seats.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` `1 Sep 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 1425 2850
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` `1 Sep 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `1 Sep 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0
-- s 97, 9 November 2026, capacity $500: (1500 - 500) x 0.8 = 800. Both seats.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` `9 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 500 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the second payment period (s 93)` 800 1600
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` `9 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 500 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `9 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 500 TRUE 12 0
-- s 98: workers compensation of $300 for a week on 15 October: 1425 - 300 = 1125.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` `15 Oct 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 300 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 1125 2250
-- 1 April 2027: not covered, both seats.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` `1 Apr 2027` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits not covered` `no deposited AWE indexed amounts for ss 96, 97 and 103 on that day (NI2026-402 covers 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027)`
-- A limitation ends the benefits: nothing to pay.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit must I pay` `1 Sep 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE TRUE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `no income replacement benefits` `a limitation in division 2.2.2 ends or excludes these benefits (ss 43 to 50)`
-- s 101: from 3 August 2026 to 3 August 2031. Both seats.
#ASSERT `For what period must I pay income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
#ASSERT `For what period must I pay income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026`
-- A late application on 1 December 2026: from 28 days before, 3 November 2026.
#ASSERT `For what period must I pay income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
-- FINDING 3: a short-hours casual: no s 101 start date, both seats.
#ASSERT `For what period must I pay income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 20 `casual short` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `period not covered` `no start date in s 101 (3) to (5) for this work situation`

-- s 103: asked 17 August 2026, nothing given; 80% (HYPOTHETICAL) of $2 794 on 20 August = 2235.20. Both seats.
#ASSERT `How much interim weekly payment may I pay` `3 Aug 2026` `17 Aug 2026` FALSE `17 Aug 2026` 80 `20 Aug 2026` EQUALS `dollars` 2235.2
#ASSERT `How much interim weekly payment may I pay` `3 Aug 2026` `17 Aug 2026` FALSE `17 Aug 2026` 80 `20 Aug 2026` EQUALS `How much interim weekly payment may the insurer pay me` `3 Aug 2026` `17 Aug 2026` FALSE `17 Aug 2026` 80 `20 Aug 2026`
-- An accident on 1 October 2026, asked 15 October, on 20 October: 80% of $2 864 = 2291.20.
#ASSERT `How much interim weekly payment may I pay` `1 Oct 2026` `15 Oct 2026` FALSE `15 Oct 2026` 80 `20 Oct 2026` EQUALS `dollars` 2291.2

-- Late application (s 59): applied 1 December 2026, explanation received that day; no response by 30 December: taken to
-- have accepted (28 days after was 29 December). Both seats.
#ASSERT `May I accept the late application` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `no response yet` `30 Dec 2026` `30 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer is taken to have accepted: no response to the explanation within 28 days (s 59 (4))`
#ASSERT `May I accept the late application` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `no response yet` `30 Dec 2026` `30 Dec 2026` EQUALS `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `no response yet` `30 Dec 2026` `30 Dec 2026`
#ASSERT `May I accept the late application` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `no response yet` `11 Dec 2026` `11 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer may accept, if satisfied the applicant has a full and satisfactory explanation (s 59 (2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- MIRROR CASE 2. Quality of life. WPI 8%, one WPI report, dated and received by the insurer on 1 October 2026; the
-- amount is as at the date of the report (s 167 (1) (b)). HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 155: 5% to 9%, must offer; notice within 14 days after receiving the report on 1 October: 15 October 2026.
#ASSERT `Which WPI notice must I give` 8 FALSE EQUALS `s 155: WPI 5% to 9%, the insurer must make an offer`
#ASSERT `Which WPI notice must I give` 8 FALSE EQUALS `What must the insurer offer me` 8 FALSE
#ASSERT `By when must I give the WPI notice` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `15 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `By when must I give the WPI notice` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `By when must the insurer give me the WPI notice` `1 Oct 2026`
-- Table 167 item 3, 1 October 2026 figures: 8960 + 3 x 2720 = 17120. Both seats.
#ASSERT `How much quality of life benefit must I offer` 8 `1 Oct 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dollars` 17120
#ASSERT `How much quality of life benefit must I offer` 8 `1 Oct 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `How much quality of life benefit do I get` 8 `1 Oct 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 133: a child taken to have 10%, assessed 3%: 22560. Both seats.
#ASSERT `How much quality of life benefit must I offer` 3 `1 Oct 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dollars` 22560
#ASSERT `How much quality of life benefit must I offer` 3 `1 Oct 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `How much quality of life benefit do I get` 3 `1 Oct 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A limitation (here s 44): nothing to offer. s 135: already received: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much quality of life benefit must I offer` 8 `1 Oct 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing payable` `a limitation in division 2.2.2 ends or excludes these benefits (ss 43 to 50)`
#ASSERT `How much quality of life benefit must I offer` 8 `1 Oct 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nothing payable` `quality of life benefits already received (s 135)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- MIRROR CASE 3. Sam dies on 10 August 2026 after an accident on 3 August 2026; a domestic partner and 2 dependent
-- children on the date of the accident. The insurer accepts liability for death benefits on Thursday 1 October 2026
-- (Labour Day, Monday 5 October, falls in the five business days). HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 176 (3): from 10 October 2026. Both seats.
#ASSERT `From when may I apply to the ACAT` `1 Oct 2026` 1 FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `10 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `From when may I apply to the ACAT` `1 Oct 2026` 1 FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `From when may the insurer apply to the ACAT for our death benefits` `1 Oct 2026` 1 FALSE `1 Oct 2026`
-- Accepted 2 November 2026, notice for information on 20 October: from 18 November 2026.
#ASSERT `From when may I apply to the ACAT` `2 Nov 2026` 0 TRUE `20 Oct 2026` EQUALS `18 Nov 2026`
-- ss 174, 177 (2): the most the ACAT can order, worked out on 15 November 2026: 242400 + 102090 = 344490. Both seats.
#ASSERT `What is the most the ACAT can order me to pay in death benefits` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 2 FALSE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `dollars` 344490
#ASSERT `What is the most the ACAT can order me to pay in death benefits` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 2 FALSE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `What death benefits are payable` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Nov 2026`
-- An order for 344490 is within the cap; 344491 is not. An exclusion: nil, so any positive order is over it.
#ASSERT `Is the ACAT order within the cap` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 2 FALSE `15 Nov 2026` 344490
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the ACAT order within the cap` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 2 FALSE `15 Nov 2026` 344491)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the ACAT order within the cap` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 2 TRUE `15 Nov 2026` 1)
#ASSERT `What is the most the ACAT can order me to pay in death benefits` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 2 TRUE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `nothing payable` `an exclusion in section 46, 49 or 170 to 173 applies (s 169 (2))`
-- s 175: both seats agree.
#ASSERT `Must I pay the estate what the person was owed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (`Must I pay the estate what the person was owed` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS (`Is the estate paid what the person was owed` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 181: expenses $25 000 on 15 November 2026: the maximum, 19160. $12 000: 12000. Both seats.
#ASSERT `What must I pay in funeral benefits` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` 25000 FALSE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `dollars` 19160
#ASSERT `What must I pay in funeral benefits` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` 25000 FALSE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `How much funeral benefit can I be paid` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` TRUE 25000 FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `What must I pay in funeral benefits` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` 12000 FALSE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `dollars` 12000
#ASSERT `What must I pay in funeral benefits` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` 12000 TRUE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `nothing payable` `an exclusion in section 49, 179 or 180 applies (s 178 (2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- REGULATIVE RULES. s 59 -> s 60 -> s 65 -> s 66 (or s 176). Mia's application: day 0 is 3 August 2026; the late
-- application limit, 3 August 2028, is day 731 (2028 is a leap year); the HYPOTHETICAL guideline period for a receipt
-- notice is 5 days. She applies on 20 August (day 17).
-- =====================================================================================================================

`Mia's application rule` MEANS `s 59 -- the application must be made within the application period, or late with an explanation` `IRB` 731 5 0

-- In time: applies day 17; receipt notice day 19 (within 5); liability accepted day 39 (within 28 of day 19); paid
-- day 50.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `Mia's application rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for defined benefits` 17), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the receipt notice` 19), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`decide liability and give notice of the decision` TRUE) 39), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `pay the defined benefits` 50)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Liability rejected on day 30: nothing more owed under this rule (review is part 2.10, not encoded).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `Mia's application rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for defined benefits` 17), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the receipt notice` 19), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`decide liability and give notice of the decision` FALSE) 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 65 (4): no decision by day 47; the insurer is taken to accept, must give a defined benefits notice and pay.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `Mia's application rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for defined benefits` 17), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the receipt notice` 19), (WAITUNTIL 48), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give a defined benefits notice` 50), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `pay the defined benefits` 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the relevant insurer, "s 60 (1): the relevant insurer must give the applicant a receipt notice ..."
-- (the receipt notice only on day 23, 6 days after the application)
#TRACE `Mia's application rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply for defined benefits` AT 17
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `give the receipt notice` AT 23
-- expect: the s 66 obligation still pending, PARTY the relevant insurer MUST pay the defined benefits (accepted, not
-- yet paid; s 66 sets no period)
#TRACE `Mia's application rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply for defined benefits` AT 17
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `give the receipt notice` AT 19
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `decide liability and give notice of the decision` TRUE AT 39
-- expect: still pending after deemed acceptance, PARTY the relevant insurer MUST give a defined benefits notice
#TRACE `Mia's application rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply for defined benefits` AT 17
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `give the receipt notice` AT 19
    (WAITUNTIL 48)

-- Late (s 59 (2)): the period ends day 90; wait to day 91; late application with explanation day 120; the insurer
-- accepts it day 130 (within 28); late receipt notice day 132; liability accepted day 140; paid day 150.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `Mia's application rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 91), (EVENT `the applicant` `make a late application with an explanation for the delay` 120), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`respond to the explanation for the late application` TRUE) 130), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the late receipt notice` 132), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`decide liability and give notice of the decision` TRUE) 140), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `pay the defined benefits` 150)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 59 (4): no response by day 148; taken to accept; late receipt notice day 150; liability accepted day 160; paid 170.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `Mia's application rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 91), (EVENT `the applicant` `make a late application with an explanation for the delay` 120), (WAITUNTIL 149), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the late receipt notice` 150), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`decide liability and give notice of the decision` TRUE) 160), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `pay the defined benefits` 170)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- The insurer refuses the late application on day 130: nothing more owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `Mia's application rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 91), (EVENT `the applicant` `make a late application with an explanation for the delay` 120), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`respond to the explanation for the late application` FALSE) 130)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 59 (5): no application by the limit (day 731): nothing owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `Mia's application rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 91), (WAITUNTIL 732)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the relevant insurer, "s 60 (1): ..." (after accepting the late application on day 130, it gave a
-- receipt notice, not a late receipt notice, and none of the right kind by day 135)
#TRACE `Mia's application rule` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 91)
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `make a late application with an explanation for the delay` AT 120
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `respond to the explanation for the late application` TRUE AT 130
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `give the receipt notice` AT 132
    (WAITUNTIL 140)

-- Death benefits (s 66 note, s 176). Sam's dependants: day 0 is the death, 10 August 2026; the late limit, 10 August
-- 2027, is day 365. They apply 10 September (day 31); receipt notice 14 September (day 35); liability accepted
-- Thursday 1 October (day 52); the ACAT application may be made from 10 October (9 days after acceptance, day 61).
`the dependants' application rule` MEANS `s 59 -- the application must be made within the application period, or late with an explanation` `death benefits` 365 5 9
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the dependants' application rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for defined benefits` 31), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the receipt notice` 35), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`decide liability and give notice of the decision` TRUE) 52), (WAITUNTIL 61), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `apply to the ACAT for an order for payment of the death benefits` 62)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: DEONTIC BREACHED, the relevant insurer did the prohibited act (MUST NOT apply to the ACAT ...) at day 55,
-- 3 days after accepting liability (the stable l4 reports a broken prohibition without its BECAUSE text)
#TRACE `the dependants' application rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply for defined benefits` AT 31
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `give the receipt notice` AT 35
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `decide liability and give notice of the decision` TRUE AT 52
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `apply to the ACAT for an order for payment of the death benefits` AT 55
-- The s 176 rule alone, 9 days: wait to day 9, apply day 10.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 176 -- the insurer must apply to the ACAT for the death benefits order, and not before the later of 5 business days and 28 days` 9) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 9), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `apply to the ACAT for an order for payment of the death benefits` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the obligation still pending, PARTY the relevant insurer MUST apply to the ACAT ... (no latest day is set)
#TRACE `s 176 -- the insurer must apply to the ACAT for the death benefits order, and not before the later of 5 business days and 28 days` 9 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 9)
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- s 102: two fortnights of $2 850, paid on days 14 and 28.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 102 -- the insurer must pay income replacement benefits every 14 days after the start date` 2 2850) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`pay the income replacement benefits for the fortnight` 2850) 14), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`pay the income replacement benefits for the fortnight` 2850) 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 102 -- the insurer must pay income replacement benefits every 14 days after the start date` 0 2850) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the relevant insurer, "s 102 (1), s 66 (1): ..." (paid $2 800, not $2 850, and nothing more by
-- day 14)
#TRACE `s 102 -- the insurer must pay income replacement benefits every 14 days after the start date` 2 2850 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `pay the income replacement benefits for the fortnight` 2800 AT 14
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- ss 154-157. Day 0: the insurer receives the WPI report. s 155, 26 weeks (182 days) to reply, $17 120.
`the s 155 notice rule` MEANS `ss 154 to 157 -- the insurer must give the WPI notice within 14 days, and the injured person's reply` `s 155: WPI 5% to 9%, the insurer must make an offer` 182 17120
-- Notice day 10; accepted day 50; paid day 60.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the s 155 notice rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the WPI notice` 10), (EVENT `the injured person` (`notify the insurer whether accepting or disagreeing with each WPI report` TRUE) 50), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`pay the quality of life benefits` 17120) 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 155 (5): silence to day 192; taken to accept; paid day 200.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the s 155 notice rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the WPI notice` 10), (WAITUNTIL 193), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`pay the quality of life benefits` 17120) 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Disagrees on day 30 (a second WPI assessment follows, s 158, not encoded).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the s 155 notice rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the WPI notice` 10), (EVENT `the injured person` (`notify the insurer whether accepting or disagreeing with each WPI report` FALSE) 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the relevant insurer, "ss 154 (3), 155 (4), 156 (4), 157 (4): ..." (notice on day 15)
#TRACE `the s 155 notice rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `give the WPI notice` AT 15
-- expect: the payment obligation still pending, PARTY the relevant insurer MUST pay the quality of life benefits 17120
-- (taken to accept on silence, not yet paid)
#TRACE `the s 155 notice rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the relevant insurer` DOES `give the WPI notice` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 193)
-- FINDING 10. s 157 (6): silence until the due date ends the entitlement; nothing is owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 154 to 157 -- the insurer must give the WPI notice within 14 days, and the injured person's reply` `s 157: WPI 10% or more, with a motor accident claim, the insurer must make an offer` 1760 38160) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the WPI notice` 10), (WAITUNTIL 1771)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 156 (5): silence is acceptance and must be paid.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 154 to 157 -- the insurer must give the WPI notice within 14 days, and the injured person's reply` `s 156: WPI 10% or more, no motor accident claim, the insurer must make an offer` 182 38160) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the WPI notice` 10), (WAITUNTIL 193), (EVENT `the relevant insurer` (`pay the quality of life benefits` 38160) 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- FINDING 10. s 154: an accepted offer carries no express duty to pay.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 154 to 157 -- the insurer must give the WPI notice within 14 days, and the injured person's reply` `s 154: WPI less than 5%, the insurer may make an offer` 182 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the relevant insurer` `give the WPI notice` 10), (EVENT `the injured person` (`notify the insurer whether accepting or disagreeing with each WPI report` TRUE) 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
